==English==

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{infl of|en|slight||ing-form}}
#: {{ux|en|His habit of '''slighting''' the company chairman was considered to be inappropriate behaviour.}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# In the manner of a [[slight]]; [[belittling]], [[deprecative]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The act of giving a [[slight]] or [[snub]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1848|author=Lucy Hutchinson|title=Memoirs of the life of Colonel Hutchinson|page=376
|passage={{...}} the rest, who had looked upon him with such disdainful neglect {{...}} now flocked about him, striving who should express most respect, and, by an extraordinary officiousness, redeem their late '''slightings'''.}}
# {{lb|en|regional}} An act of ignoring or neglecting someone or something; more broadly [[neglect]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''slighting''' of children}}
# {{lb|en|regional}} The action of rejecting someone or something; [[rejection|rejection]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''slighting''' of a handshake by Samuel ticked off Judi to no end.}}
# {{lb|en|military}} The full or partial demolition of a fortification.

